{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\n[S01] designates the Incident Commander (IC) as the sole authority for evacuation orders. [S02] confirms IC approval is required for cancellation, which needs field confirmation. Vendors and dashboards are advisory only [S01].\n*   **Disposition:** Bound.\n*   **Blockers:** None.\n\n**R02: Hazard Triggers & Zone Sequencing**\n[S02] defines conservative triggers: Zone A mandatory <6h or spotting across Dry Creek; Zone B mandatory <5h, prepare >9h. The governing trigger is the conservative envelope (5.8h for Zone A), not the median (7.5h) [S02]. Forecast updates accelerate orders but cannot silently cancel them [S02].\n*   **Disposition:** Bound.\n*   **Qualifications:** Use conservative ensemble, not median [S02].\n*   **Blockers:** None.\n\n**R03: Population Basis & Assistance Demand**\n[S03] lists Zone A (5,280), B (8,940), C (12,600) residents plus up to 2,100 tourists [S03]. Medical categories (no vehicle, mobility, oxygen, dialysis) overlap and must not be summed as independent people [S03]. Survey coverage is 91%; an uncertainty allowance is required for unreported households [S03].\n*   **Disposition:** Bound.\n*   **Qualifications:** Do not sum overlapping medical categories as separate individuals [S03]. Tourist demand is time-dependent [S03].\n*   **Blockers:** None.\n\n**R04: Road Bottlenecks & Route Clearance**\n[S04] identifies Mill Junction as the bottleneck (1,500 veh/h). North Bridge (1,100 veh/h) and South Pass (850 veh/h) feed into it; capacities cannot be added [S04]. Exercise throughput was 1,180 veh/h [S04]. Contraflow requires sheriff closure and 45 minutes setup [S04].\n*   **Disposition:** Bound.\n*   **Qualifications:** Do not sum roads sharing Mill Junction [S04]. Use exercise throughput until field-tested otherwise [S04].\n*   **Blockers:** None.\n\n**R05: Fleet Matching & Driver Duty**\n[S03] requires fleet reservation by person/accommodation, not household count [S03]. [S16] lists \"complete driver roster\" as a blocker but provides no operational data [S16]. No evidence for driver duty cycles or relief capacity exists in allowed sources.\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** No fleet matching logic or driver duty data in [S03], [S04], [S16].\n\n**R06: Shelter Capacity & Medical Handoffs**\n[S11] establishes that PM2.5 >150 µg/m³ triggers relocation of unfiltered shelters, and >250 µg/m³ requires respiratory protection [S11]. Ridge School failed its last filter inspection; Civic Arena and West College passed with MERV-13 filters; Expo Hall has only 80% of required replacement filters on site [S11]. Shelter capacity must be recalculated under air-quality forecast, not nominal building occupancy [S11]. Medical cohorts have lower exposure tolerance [S11]. [S02] notes air-quality shelter viability can remove destinations, altering road demand [S02].\n*   **Disposition:** Partially Bound.\n*   **Qualifications:** Do not declare clean-air capacity from nominal building occupancy [S11]. Filter replacement requires a current inspection, not reuse of prior readiness check [S11]. Distance from flame is not a complete shelter-safety criterion [S11].\n*   **Blockers:** Ridge School filter repair incomplete [S16]; person-level oxygen matching unresolved [S16]; no operational medical handoff protocol in allowed sources.\n\n**R07: Warnings & Community Support**\n[S16] lists \"volunteer-radio identifier test\" as a blocker but provides no operational data [S16]. No evidence for multilingual warning, door-knock timing, or receipt/understanding evidence exists in allowed sources.\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind communication strategy [S16].\n\n**R08: Fuel & Power Continuity**\n[S16] lists \"alternate fuel confirmation\" as a blocker but provides no operational data [S16]. No evidence for observed delays, local staging, or coupled asset effects exists in allowed sources.\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind resource contracting [S16].\n\n**R09: Animals & Service Animals**\n[S10] estimates 1,480 household pets in Zones A and B; pet-capable shelter space is 600 [S10]. Fourteen livestock trailers move 112 large animals per cycle; registry lists 320 in the threatened area [S10]. Service animals remain with handlers and count against neither pet shelter nor livestock capacity [S10]. Human evacuation may not be held until every animal is moved [S10]. Animal trailers compete with buses at Mill Junction and require different shelter destinations [S10].\n*   **Disposition:** Partially Bound.\n*   **Qualifications:** Do not double-count service animals against pet or livestock capacity [S10]. Provide parallel animal plan without delaying human movement [S10]. Public messaging must distinguish categories so capacity is not double-counted [S10].\n*   **Blockers:** Pet shelter deficit of 880 (1,480 demand vs. 600 capacity) [S10]; livestock deficit of 208 (320 demand vs. 112 per cycle) [S10]; no documented last-safe transport time or overflow agreements in allowed sources.\n\n**R10: Accountability & Data Privacy**\nNo evidence for private accountability, public aggregation, restricted health data handling, reconciliation, retention, or deletion proof is present in allowed sources.\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind data management protocol.\n\n**R11: 48-Hour Execution Sequence**\nNo evidence for a concrete 48-hour sequence with owners, effects, current checks, repair, recheck, resource/cost authority, and contingencies is present in allowed sources. [S16] classifies the package as not ready due to open blockers [S16].\n*   **Disposition:** Missing.\n*   **Blockers:** Cannot bind execution timeline [S16].\n\n**R12: Verification & Readiness Blockers**\n[S16] classifies the package as not ready. Open blockers include North Bridge engineering inspection, complete driver roster, Ridge School filter repair, volunteer-radio identifier test, alternate fuel confirmation, and person-level oxygen matching [S16]. Component dashboards are green but bind to different plan revisions; no current integrated check exists [S16]. Readiness requires every hard blocker resolved, effects incorporated, a current integrated exercise or justified bounded check, and incident-command acceptance [S16]. Submission or a model-authored ledger cannot create that authority [S16].\n*   **Disposition:** Not Ready.\n*   **Blockers:** All six blockers in [S16] remain open; pet/livestock overflow agreements undocumented [S10].\n\n**Cross-Source Relationships & Contradictions**\n[S03] defines demand; [S04] defines supply constraints; [S01] defines authority; [S16] defines readiness status; [S10] defines animal logistics constraints; [S11] defines air-quality shelter viability. No contradictions exist between these sources. However, all lack evidence for fleet specifics (R05), communications (R07), resources (R08), data privacy (R10), and execution sequence (R11). The integration is incomplete for a full evacuation decision.\n\n**Unresolved Evidence**\n*   Fleet matching logic linking [S03] demand to vehicle capacity is absent.\n*   Shelter location and capacity data beyond air-quality status are missing from provided sources.\n*   Multilingual warning, door-knock timing, and receipt/understanding evidence are entirely absent."}}],"created":1787627940,"model":"Qwen3.8-27B-AD-IQ2_S.gguf","system_fingerprint":"b10434-7e4c0a968","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":1822,"prompt_tokens":6423,"total_tokens":8245,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-KN7xQZDcgRVWYY5BML2UH0LO6lJGAIh7","__verbose":{"index":0,"content":"# Evidence Integration Ledger\n\n**R01: Legal Order & Authority**\n[S01] designates the Incident Commander (IC) as the sole authority for evacuation orders. [S02] confirms IC approval is required for ca